<section class="work-panel" id="fabrication-panel"><div class="panel-title"><h2>Selected member · pieces and assembly</h2><button id="export-proposed-bbs" type="button">Download selected BBS · CSV</button></div><div class="v3-section-body"><div id="proposal-status" aria-live="polite"></div><div id="confinement-check"></div><div id="proposed-bbs"></div><div class="v5-shape-controls"><label>Dimensioned piece<select id="shape-select"></select></label><button id="export-proposed-shape" type="button">Download piece · SVG</button></div><div class="v6-drawing-pair"><div id="fabrication-shape" class="v5-shape"></div><div id="assembly-shape" class="v5-shape"></div></div><details><summary>Exact tangent and arc calculation</summary><div id="shape-segments"></div></details><details><summary>Lap fit and anchorage comparison</summary><div id="lap-fit"></div><p>Source 60φ in sheet 9 refers to the horizontal starter-bar anchorage leg; it is not the whole starter cut or a blanket footing-mesh length. The source stair development1,570 mm remains separate.</p></details><details><summary>Selected-member stock packing · beam pieces only</summary><div id="stock-packing"></div></details><p><a href="./data/proposed-bbs.csv">All-member BBS · CSV</a> · <a href="./data/member-checks.json">Checks · JSON</a> · <a href="./design-basis.json">Decision basis · JSON</a></p><a class="contents-return" href="#page-contents">Contents ↑</a></div></section>
<section class="work-panel" id="connection-panel"><div class="panel-title"><h2>Column connections · measured coordination</h2><button id="download-connections" type="button">Download connection study · JSON</button></div><div class="v3-section-body"><p>Choose <strong>Column cages</strong> and a named column in the work filters. The two groups each contain half of its steel area. Their sleeve envelopes are checked against the actual modelled hoops.</p><div id="connection-status" aria-live="polite"></div><label class="v6-selector">Connection to highlight<select id="connection-select"></select></label><div class="v6-connection-layout"><div id="connection-drawing" class="v5-shape"></div><div id="connection-table"></div></div><details><summary>Product, transition and end-preparation evidence</summary><div id="connection-evidence"></div></details><p><a href="./data/column-connections.json">All column studies · JSON</a> · <a href="./data/column-connections.csv">All connection coordinates · CSV</a></p><a class="contents-return" href="#page-contents">Contents ↑</a></div></section>
<section class="work-panel" id="renderer-check"><div class="panel-title"><h2>3D view · reliable default</h2><button id="run-3d-check" type="button">Check current 3D view</button></div><div class="v3-section-body"><p>The default uses the same Three.js scene, orthographic camera and orbit controls, projected into SVG. It supports rotation, zoom, selection and dimensions without requiring WebGL. Optional WebGL can be tried on this device.</p><details><summary>Renderer observations and optional WebGL</summary><div id="renderer-results" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="v5-button-row"><button id="use-vector" type="button">Use vector 3D</button><button id="retry-webgl" type="button">Try optional WebGL</button><button id="test-context-loss" type="button">Test WebGL context loss</button><button id="download-renderer-report" type="button">Download device report · JSON</button></div></details></div></section>
